Subject: [PATCH] sycl: GGML_SYCL_LOCAL_OFF, one off switch per local optimization

Most local patches (ZZ-LOCAL-0003 to 0016) change a kernel choice or add a graph fusion with no way to
turn it off but GGML_SYCL_ENABLE_FUSION=0 or GGML_SYCL_ENABLE_OPT=0, which also turn off upstream's
fusions and reorders. They are stacked (0016 extends 0013's epilogue, 0012 and 0015 extend 0011's
matchers), so a build without one of them would need regenerated patches, and a rebuild between the A and
B runs of a benchmark adds build and thermal drift. GGML_SYCL_LOCAL_OFF=<decimal mask> turns them off one
bit at a time in the same binary; a set bit restores the path the backend took before that patch:

    1      0003  2..8-column MMVQ of IQ1 / IQ2 / IQ4_NL / IQ3_XXS in the block layout
    2      0004, 0007, 0008  per-expert reorder of q4_0 / q2_K / q3_K / iq4_nl / iq3_xxs / iq3_s experts
    4      0007  dense iq4_nl reorder
    8      0010  gate + up MMVQ pairs rows on the A-series again (the spilling variants)
    16     0011  ROPE + VIEW + SET_ROWS
    32     0011  RMS_NORM + MUL + ROPE (+ VIEW + SET_ROWS)
    64     0011  MoE weighted expert sum
    128    0011  chains of 3..8 ADDs
    256    0011, 0015  topk-moe with a routing bias, sqrt(softplus) gating or expert groups
    512    0012  MUL_MAT_ID gate + up + GLU and the MUL_MAT_ID + ADD_ID epilogue
    1024   0013  MUL_MAT + ADD (0016's MMVQ epilogue with it)
    2048   0014  sibling mat-muls share the converted activation
    4096   0015  softcap, relu^2, snake, the DSV4_HC_POST gate, SSM_SCAN writing the cache
    8192   0016  the MMVQ add epilogue only (0013 then adds in place after the mat-vec)
    16384  candidate C10's iq4_xs reorder (no effect without C10)

0012's 2..8-token MoE MMVQ already has GGML_SYCL_MMID_MMVQ_MAX_TOKENS=1, 0017 is opt-in
(GGML_SYCL_XMX_GRF256), and 0010's 8-row GEMM tile is a compile-time shape whose alternative is 0017's
tile. The matchers that graph_optimize also calls (0012, 0013, 0011's expert sum) test their bit inside,
so a disabled fusion also drops the allocation dependencies it adds. The default 0 changes nothing.

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/common.hpp b/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/common.hpp
index dd881fba..a8886ef5 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/common.hpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/common.hpp
@@ -78,6 +78,32 @@ extern int g_ggml_sycl_xmx_max_cols;
 extern int g_ggml_sycl_xmx_glu_max_cols;
 extern int g_ggml_sycl_prioritize_dmmv;
 
+// Off switches for the local patches (ZZ-LOCAL-*) that have none of their own, one bit each, so one build can
+// A/B every one of them: GGML_SYCL_LOCAL_OFF=<mask>, 0 (the default) keeps them all on. A set bit restores the
+// path the backend took before that patch.
+enum ggml_sycl_local_off_bit {
+    GGML_SYCL_LOCAL_OFF_IQ_NCOLS        = 1 << 0,   // 0003: 2..8-column MMVQ of IQ1 / IQ2 / IQ4_NL / IQ3_XXS (block layout)
+    GGML_SYCL_LOCAL_OFF_MOE_REORDER     = 1 << 1,   // 0004, 0007, 0008: per-expert reorder of q4_0 / q2_K / q3_K / iq4_nl / iq3
+    GGML_SYCL_LOCAL_OFF_IQ4_NL_REORDER  = 1 << 2,   // 0007: dense iq4_nl reorder
+    GGML_SYCL_LOCAL_OFF_DG2_GLU_ONE_ROW = 1 << 3,   // 0010: gate + up MMVQ pairs rows on the A-series again
+    GGML_SYCL_LOCAL_OFF_ROPE_SET_ROWS   = 1 << 4,   // 0011: ROPE + VIEW + SET_ROWS
+    GGML_SYCL_LOCAL_OFF_NORM_ROPE       = 1 << 5,   // 0011: RMS_NORM + MUL + ROPE (+ VIEW + SET_ROWS)
+    GGML_SYCL_LOCAL_OFF_MOE_SUM         = 1 << 6,   // 0011: MoE weighted expert sum
+    GGML_SYCL_LOCAL_OFF_MULTI_ADD       = 1 << 7,   // 0011: chains of 3..8 ADDs
+    GGML_SYCL_LOCAL_OFF_TOPK_MOE_EXT    = 1 << 8,   // 0011, 0015: topk-moe with a routing bias, sqrt(softplus) or groups
+    GGML_SYCL_LOCAL_OFF_MOE_MMVQ_FUSE   = 1 << 9,   // 0012: MUL_MAT_ID gate + up + GLU and the ADD_ID epilogue
+    GGML_SYCL_LOCAL_OFF_MUL_MAT_ADD     = 1 << 10,  // 0013 (and 0016): MUL_MAT + ADD
+    GGML_SYCL_LOCAL_OFF_ACT_REUSE       = 1 << 11,  // 0014: sibling mat-muls share the converted activation
+    GGML_SYCL_LOCAL_OFF_MODEL_FUSIONS   = 1 << 12,  // 0015: softcap, relu^2, snake, DSV4_HC_POST gate, SSM_SCAN cache
+    GGML_SYCL_LOCAL_OFF_MMVQ_ADD        = 1 << 13,  // 0016: the MMVQ add epilogue (0013's in-place ADD instead)
+    GGML_SYCL_LOCAL_OFF_IQ4_XS_REORDER  = 1 << 14,  // candidate C10: iq4_xs reorder
+};
+extern int g_ggml_sycl_local_off;
+
+static inline bool ggml_sycl_local_on(int bit) {
+    return (g_ggml_sycl_local_off & bit) == 0;
+}
